From f526cbd81c40a419ec648d8b9c802e70924cdc0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teemu Haila <teemu.haila@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:45:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/36] iMac 5K: drop the cached peer stream before the resume
 commit

[upstream: imac5k-universal-linux-patcher patches/5k-resume-drop-cached-peer.patch @ c1086d2b438c]
Applied unchanged with patch -p1 onto v7.2.11-arch1 + probe-defer.

dm_destroy_cached_state() releases every cached CRTC's stream and every
cached plane's dc_state (and dc_state_peer) so that the resume commit's
atomic check builds fresh ones. It left the stitched root CRTC's stream_peer
in place. The resume commit starts from the suspended state, whose CRTC has no
stream, so the disable pass never runs and the stale peer survives into the
enable pass. There the stitch gate sees stream_peer already set and skips
creating a new peer, the root is added to a fresh DC context without it, and
the plane split then fails:

  dc_state_add_plane: Existing stream not found; failed to attach surface!

drm_atomic_helper_resume() returns -EINVAL, which dm_resume() ignores, and
the cached peer stream's reference leaks. The panel only came back because a
later hotplug commit, built from the suspended state, took the normal path.

Seen on iMac18,3, kernel 7.2.3, lean stack + 5k-logical-modeset-guard,
2026-09-10: pm_test=devices (deep). This is the first devices-level resume in
the retained journal, so it is not tied to the guard, which only acts when the
old state still holds a stream.

Release the peer next to the root stream, as the plane loop already does for
dc_state_peer.

Applies on top of either stack: this loop is mainline code in both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SUvgXxxT5Apr7YLjKZVd2T
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
index 6c41484a2..ddaa66f80 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -4255,6 +4255,11 @@ static void dm_destroy_cached_state(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 			dc_stream_release(dm_new_crtc_state->stream);
 			dm_new_crtc_state->stream = NULL;
 		}
+		/* tiled stitch: release the cached peer (right-tile) stream too. */
+		if (dm_new_crtc_state->stream_peer) {
+			dc_stream_release(dm_new_crtc_state->stream_peer);
+			dm_new_crtc_state->stream_peer = NULL;
+		}
 		dm_new_crtc_state->base.color_mgmt_changed = true;
 	}
 
